      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-11T09:41:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you need PV support, please use the existing in-kernel interface to support a PV system.  That should not require random hooks in individual drivers like this, but it should be either specific drivers for your platform (which you can do with a UFS driver here), or core kernel changes that happen at boot time based on your hardware platform.  Linux already supports both of these, no need for random UFS core hooks.",
      "parentUuid": "1e1a91b6_b1295a68",
      "revId": "fa0198c410d70ada681747ddca029407033b559a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
